        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lands Moanarone, Old Quay Road, Bandon, Co Cork, \r\nc.0.39 ha - c. 0.96 acres \r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 14th of October 2026 \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Potential \r\n\r\nLocation Bandon, Innishannon 6km, Kinsale 19km, Cork City 29km. \r\n\r\nThe lands are superbly located on Mill Road accessed from the N71, 1km east of the centre of Bandon town. Population (2022) 8,196. Bandon is a town known as the Gateway to West Cork. It lies on the River Bandon between two hills. Bandon is 27 km southwest of Cork City, on the N71, and served by Bus Éireann bus services from Cork city. The nearest airport is Cork Airport, 27km. There are 4 primary and secondary schools in the town, an array of shops, restaurants, cafes and sporting clubs. Bandon is widely regarded as a practical and appealing commuter town with a strong community feel. It offers easy access to stunning nearby beaches, coastal villages like Kinsale and Clonakilty, and scenic countryside, and is within easy reach of Cork city. \r\n\r\nDescription Folio CK84181F\r\n\r\nThe lands are contained within folio CK84181F and amount to c.0.39 ha - c. 0.96 acres. The subject lands are in one irregular shaped block. They are laid out in large open plan manageable division, with mature boundaries of hedging and trees. The lands are currently in grass of good quality, however presently, are overgrown in areas. There is good road frontage. \r\n\r\nIdeal location for a one-off property, subject to the necessary planning. \r\n\r\nThe lands are being sold as seen and not subject to planning. \r\n\r\nCoordinates 51.747109, -8.718347\r\n\r\nViewing By Appointment Only\r\n\r\nSolicitor Gabriel Motea, Byrne Wallace Shields, 88 Harcourt Street, Dublin 2\r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
